    "body": "TitanRL independently defaults both allocator configuration names. Setting only `PYTORCH_ALLOC_CONF=expandable_segments:False` therefore adds `PYTORCH_CUDA_ALLOC_CONF=expandable_segments:True`, which PyTorch reads first and uses instead of the explicit setting.\n\nCopy an explicit CUDA/unified value into the missing alias before applying defaults. Preserve empty values, both explicitly supplied values, and the existing late-import warning. Defaults are unchanged when neither alias is set.\n\nValidation: eight CPU tests pass; four alias regressions fail on main. Three alternating baseline/candidate comparisons of actual H100 CUDA allocator snapshots confirm the fix with PyTorch 2.9.0+cu130. Applicable pinned file hooks pass; the unavailable global Pyrefly checker excludes both changed paths.\n\nPrepared with AI assistance.\n",
